--- a/build/manifold-src/src/parallel.h
+++ b/build/manifold-src/src/parallel.h
@@ -647,8 +647,9 @@ void exclusive_scan(ExecutionPolicy policy, InputIter first, InputIter last,
   (void)identity;
 #endif
   for (; first != last; ++first, ++d_first) {
-    *d_first = init;
-    init = f(init, *first);
+    auto cur = *first;  // read BEFORE write — fixes aliased/in-place usage
+    *d_first = init;
+    init = f(init, cur);
   }
 }

Bug: the sequential exclusive_scan wrote *d_first before reading *first.
When the input iterator aliases the output buffer (as in quickhull.cpp's
  exclusive_scan(TransformIterator(counts.begin(), saturate),
                 TransformIterator(counts.end(), saturate), counts.begin(), 0)
the scan reads back its own output instead of the original counts, making
every output element 0.  This caused Manifold::Hull() to always return an
empty mesh.

Fix: save *first before overwriting *d_first.

Apply this patch after downloading/extracting the manifold source:
  patch -p1 < manifold-hull-fix.patch
from the build/ directory.
